# Normalize line endings to LF in both the repository and the working tree.
#
# This project is worked on from Linux/WSL. The `eol=lf` rule takes precedence
# over the global `core.autocrlf`, so git never converts files to CRLF even if
# the system-wide configuration asks for it.
#
# `text=auto` lets git detect binary content and leave it untouched: text files
# are normalized to LF, while binary assets (images, videos) are left intact.
* text=auto eol=lf
